cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "KinSim: PacBio HiFi kinetic signal generator for methylation-aware metagenomic binning"
message: "If you use KinSim in your work, please cite this software."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dutilleux
    given-names: Nicolas
    affiliation: "University of Fribourg"
    email: nicolas.dutilleux@unifr.ch
repository-code: "https://github.com/NicolasDutilleux/KinSim"
url: "https://github.com/NicolasDutilleux/KinSim"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-05-28
keywords:
  - PacBio
  - kinetics
  - methylation
  - metagenomics
  - generative model
  - bioinformatics
abstract: >
  KinSim is a generative tool that injects biologically realistic PacBio HiFi
  kinetic signals (Inter-Pulse Duration and Pulse Width) into a target BAM,
  conditioned on the local sequence context and per-position methylation
  state. It is a conditional WGAN-GP with a transformer generator and a
  transformer critic, trained on real bystrandified BAMs from production
  Streptomyces and Vega corpora and validated end-to-end through the
  PacBio analytical chain (ccs-kinetics-bystrandify, pbmm2, ipdSummary,
  pbmotifmaker, jasmine, modkit).
